The '''[[2020–21 in Scottish football|2020–21 season]]''' was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 127th season of competitive football. They competed in the [[2020–21 Scottish Premiership|Scottish Premiership]], [[2020–21 Scottish Cup|Scottish Cup]], [[2020–21 Scottish League Cup|League Cup]], [[2020–21 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]] and [[2020–21 UEFA Europa League|UEFA Europa League]]. The club failed to win a trophy for first time since 2010.

==Pre-season and friendlies==
Celtic held a pre-season training camp in Loughborough (England), before continuing their preparations in France with friendlies against [[OGC Nice|Nice]], [[Olympique Lyonnais|Lyon]] and [[Paris Saint-Germain F.C.|Paris Saint-Germain]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.com/news/18301 | title=Neil Lennon: players' pre-season progress is going well | publisher=Celtic FC | date=8 July 2020 | access-date=9 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.com/news/18309 | title=Celtic to take on top French sides in pre-season build-up | publisher=Celtic FC | date=10 July 2020 | access-date=10 July 2020}}</ref> They rounded off pre-season with friendlies against [[Ross County F.C.|Ross County]] and [[Hibernian F.C.|Hibernian]] at [[Celtic Park]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.com/news/18349 | title=The champions return to Paradise with pre-season double-header | publisher=Celtic FC | date=24 July 2020 | access-date=24 July 2020}}</ref>

