==UEFA Champions League==
{{Main|2020–21 UEFA Champions League}}
Celtic entered the Champions League at the first qualifying round. Due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]], all qualifiers were played as one-legged ties.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/53706842 | title=Which teams await Scottish sides in Europe? | publisher=BBC Sport| date=8 August 2020 | access-date=9 August 2020}}</ref>

===First qualifying round===
On 9 August, Celtic were drawn to face [[Knattspyrnufélag Reykjavíkur|KR Reykjavík]] (Iceland) in the first qualifying round of the [[2020–21 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.com/news/18411 | title=Celtic face KR Reykjavik in UEFA Champions League | publisher=Celtic FC | date=9 August 2020 | access-date=9 August 2020}}</ref>

